for this review said not to.\n\n## Info\n\n### IN-01: Commit authorship is a placeholder identity, not the operator's personal identity\n\n**File:** git metadata, all 9 commits in `main..HEAD`\n**Evidence:** every commit has author and committer `DevFlow Probe <devflow-probe@localhost>`. The global identity (`Dennis Kim <<email>>`, signing key path `~/.ssh/github_ed25519.pub`) is in git config only. It does not appear in any commit or tracked file. Commit trailers contain only `Co-Authored-By: Claude ... <<email>>`.\n**Issue:** None. Reported as a negative result: no personal email or local home path is in the pushed metadata. The only email-shaped strings in the full patch text are the two `<email>` trailers.\n**Fix:** None needed.\n\n### IN-02: `probe/budget.py` has no security surface; one design note\n\n**File:** `probe/budget.py:5-10`\n**Evidence:** the file holds a constant `120` and a pure function `start_secs + 120`. It does no I/O, parsing, subprocess calls, `eval`, or environment reads. It has no secrets or paths.\n**Issue:** `deadline_after` does not validate its input, for example NaN, inf, or negative values. This is not exploitable here because nothing reads external input. If a later caller passes a value from the network or from config, a NaN deadline would make `now < deadline` always false and retries would end at once. A corresponding inf would remove the retry limit. This is a robustness note, not a defect today.\n**Fix:** None required now. If the value ever comes from outside, reject it with `math.isfinite` before use.\n\n## What was searched\n\n| Check | Method | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| Secret scan, history | `gitleaks git --redact` | 10 commits scanned (incl. base commit), no leaks |\n| Secret scan, working tree | `gitleaks dir --redact .` | no leaks |\n| Independent count | rg over the full `git log -p main..HEAD` text (689 lines): `sk-`, `ghp_`/`gho_`/..., `AKIA`, `xox`, `AIza`, PEM headers, JWT `eyJ`, `password/secret/api_key/token/bear