so this is not a false claim. The `created` date also changed from 2026-09-28 to 2026-11-02 without comment; the new date matches the git history.\n**Fix:** Word it as \"automated audit only; no human sign-off. Open: UAT test 1.\"\n\n### IN-05: STATE reports resume-only time as the plan's duration\n\n**File:** `.planning/STATE.md`, against `01-01-SUMMARY.md:49,60`\n**Issue:** STATE records \"1 min\", but SUMMARY says that covers only the resume and that Task 1's time was not measured.\n**Fix:** Add the qualifier or leave the cell blank.\n\n### IN-06: No CI or repository-level secret scanning\n\n**File:** repository as a whole\n**Issue:** The repository has no CI workflow, tracked pre-commit hook or dependency manifest. Tests and secret scans run only when someone runs them by hand.\n**Fix:** If this repository outlives the probe, add a tracked `gitleaks` pre-commit hook and a workflow that runs the test suite.\n\n### IN-07: Tests depend on the working directory and repeat the offered values\n\n**File:** `tests/test_budget.py:5`, `tests/`\n**Issue:** `tests/` has no `__init__.py`, and imports resolve only when run from the repository root; running elsewhere fails visibly rather than passing. The offered values also appear in the test, REQUIREMENTS and the plan, so a human choosing another value would have to update all three.\n**Fix:** None needed now. Document \"run from the repository root\" if more tests are added.\n\n---\n\n_Reviewed: 2026-11-02T11:52:35Z_\n_Reviewer: Claude (gsd-code-reviewer, five finder passes merged by the orchestrator)_\n_Depth: deep_\n"}}}
