 on the agent-chosen budget (WR-02)\n\nThe generalist pass rated WR-02 Critical because the plan's Task 1 is `gate=\"blocking-human\"`, no human answered it, and the agent's choice of 120 stands. The doc-accuracy and external-state passes rated the same facts Warning.\n\nThis merge rates it **Warning**, for these reasons:\n- The reviewer rubric reserves Critical for security vulnerabilities, data loss, crashes and authentication or authorization bypasses in the code. This code has none of those, and it meets BUDGET-01 as written.\n- The claim that the PR would make the decision \"look human-approved\" did not hold up. SUMMARY, VERIFICATION, UAT and STATE all record it as an agent decision.\n- The gate is not bypassed. VERIFICATION is `human_needed`, `verification.status` returns `human_needed`, and the ship workflow refuses that status.\n\n**What this ruling does not change:** the human decision is still open. Nothing in this review confirms that 120 is right for the real upstream.\n\n### Scope and method\n\n- GSD's incremental scope was empty, because only planning files changed since the previous review. It would have skipped the review, so the scope was set by hand to the whole phase.\n- Planning documents, normally excluded, were included because the doc-accuracy and external-state angles need them.\n- Five finder passes ran in parallel: doc accuracy, security and leaked data, CI and build correctness, external-state claims, and a generalist deep pass. The merge re-checked the timestamps, ignore rules, `Deviations` text, NaN behaviour and verification status directly. Finder results for mutants and remote state are reported as they ran them.\n\n### What was checked and came back clean\n\n- **Secrets:** `gitleaks git --redact` (10 commits) and `gitleaks dir` found no leaks. A separate `rg` pass over `git log -p main..HEAD` found no credentials, home paths or personal emails. A planted path and a planted fake token both tripped the `rg` patterns. Pattern scanners 