ter reviewing what it holds.\n\n### WR-10: Zero discovered tests only fail on Python 3.12 or newer, and no interpreter is pinned\n\n**File:** repository as a whole; verify command at `01-01-PLAN.md:67`\n**Issue:** With an empty `tests/`, a misnamed file or a class that is not a `TestCase`, the command exited 5 on Python 3.15.2. That exit status was added in 3.12, so older interpreters would exit 0, and nothing pins the version. An all-skipped suite exits 0 on every version, though no test skips today. The repository has no CI, so these runs are manual.\n**Fix:** Pin the interpreter (for example `.python-version`) to 3.12 or newer, and assert the test count if the command is ever scripted.\n\n## Info\n\n### IN-01: `deadline_after` does not say which clock `start_secs` is on\n\n**File:** `probe/budget.py:8-10`\n**Issue:** The result is only meaningful against the same clock as the input. Mixing `time.monotonic()` and `time.time()` gives a silently wrong deadline, and wall-clock time can step.\n**Fix:** State in the docstring that both values must come from one clock, and recommend `time.monotonic()`.\n\n### IN-02: Docstring leaves open whether the deadline bounds an in-flight call\n\n**File:** `probe/budget.py:9`\n**Issue:** A call started just before the deadline with no per-call timeout could run past 240 seconds, which would defeat the comment's stated purpose. No caller exists yet.\n**Fix:** State that callers must cap each attempt at the remaining budget, or add a per-attempt timeout when the retry loop is written.\n\n### IN-03: STATE.md labels the phase several ways\n\n**File:** `.planning/STATE.md:5,14,23`\n**Issue:** The frontmatter says `status: verifying` and `percent: 0`, the body says `EXECUTING`, and the next line says \"Phase complete — ready for verification\". None of these should be read as a pass.\n**Fix:** Let GSD regenerate the file once the UAT item is answered.\n\n### IN-04: VALIDATION's wording can be read as a human sign-off\n\n**File:** `.plan